<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK nonprofits and charities operate under relentless pressure: rising demand for services, flat or declining funding, and increasing scrutiny of impact and efficiency. Every pound spent on admin is a pound not spent on the mission. AI is helping charities do more with limited resources, freeing staff for frontline work whilst improving fundraising, compliance, and reporting.</p>
<p>Generic AI tools don't understand the charity sector. They don't know what gift aid is or how to process it. They can't produce impact reports that satisfy funders' specific requirements. They don't understand the sensitivity of beneficiary data or the ethical considerations of using AI in a charitable context. A generic donor segmentation tool treats supporters like retail customers, missing the relationships and emotional connections that drive charitable giving.</p>
<p>Bespoke AI solutions are built around your mission and your data. We train donor segmentation models on your supporter database, accounting for giving patterns, campaign responses, and engagement signals unique to your cause. We build gift aid automation that integrates with your CRM and HMRC submission processes. We create impact reporting that pulls from your programme data and produces narratives in the formats your funders actually require.</p>
<p>Compliance and ethics are paramount in the charity sector. Beneficiary data is highly sensitive and protected by UK GDPR. AI systems that process this data must have appropriate legal bases, data protection impact assessments, and reliable security. We build with privacy by design, and we can implement solutions that keep sensitive data within your own infrastructure. We also help you navigate the ethical dimensions of AI in charitable work, ensuring transparency with donors and beneficiaries about how AI is used.</p>
<p>We worked with a UK disability charity with 15 staff and an annual income of £2.1m. Gift aid claims were manual and inconsistent, with an estimated 12% of eligible donations going unclaimed. Our AI gift aid automation, integrated with their CRM, increased claim rates to 98% of eligible donations within the first quarter, generating an additional £14,000 in the first year. The donor segmentation tool enabled a targeted campaign to lapsed mid-value donors that achieved a 28% reactivation rate, compared to 8% from their previous generic appeals. Impact reporting automation reduced the time spent on funder reports from three days to four hours per quarter.</p>

